-```
-
-## Button Constants
-
-### Digital Buttons (wButtons bitmask)
-
-```c
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_DPAD_UP         0x0001
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_DPAD_DOWN       0x0002
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_DPAD_LEFT       0x0004
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_DPAD_RIGHT      0x0008
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_START            0x0010
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_BACK             0x0020
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_LEFT_THUMB       0x0040    // Left stick click
-XBOX_GAMEPAD_RIGHT_THUMB      0x0080    // Right stick click
-```
-
-### Analog Buttons (bAnalogButtons[] indices)
-
-The original Xbox had pressure-sensitive face buttons (0-255):
-
-```c
-XBOX_BUTTON_A          0    // Also used for "boost" in racing games
-XBOX_BUTTON_B          1
-XBOX_BUTTON_X          2
-XBOX_BUTTON_Y          3
-XBOX_BUTTON_BLACK      4    // No equivalent on modern controllers
-XBOX_BUTTON_WHITE      5    // No equivalent on modern controllers
-XBOX_BUTTON_LTRIGGER   6    // Left trigger
-XBOX_BUTTON_RTRIGGER   7    // Right trigger
-
-XBOX_ANALOG_BUTTON_THRESHOLD  30   // Recommended press threshold
-```
-
-### Xbox → Modern Controller Mapping
-
-| Xbox Button | XInput Equivalent | Notes |
-|-------------|------------------|-------|
-| A | A | Green button |
-| B | B | Red button |
-| X | X | Blue button |
-| Y | Y | Yellow button |
-| Black | Right Bumper | Mapped to RB |
-| White | Left Bumper | Mapped to LB |
-| L Trigger | Left Trigger | Analog 0-255 |
-| R Trigger | Right Trigger | Analog 0-255 |
-| Start | Start/Menu | |
-| Back | Back/View | |
-| D-pad | D-pad | Digital only |
-| L Stick | L Stick | Click = L3 |
-| R Stick | R Stick | Click = R3 |
-
-## Ports
-
-```c
-#define XBOX_MAX_CONTROLLERS  4   // Ports 0-3
-```
-
-The Xbox supports 4 controllers. Each port can have a controller with optional memory units and other accessories. This layer only handles the gamepad; memory unit emulation is not needed for recompiled games.
+# Xbox input compatibility
+
+The Windows backend uses XInput. macOS and other SDL hosts use SDL2's mapped
+GameController API, including Xbox One/Series controllers and PS5 DualSense.
+Pair wireless controllers in the host OS before using them. SDL supplies device
+mappings; `SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG` can override a mapping if needed.
+
+| Original Xbox | Xbox One / Series | DualSense |
+|---|---|---|
+| A / B / X / Y | A / B / X / Y | Cross / Circle / Square / Triangle |
+| Black / White | RB / LB | R1 / L1 |
+| Left / right trigger | LT / RT | L2 / R2 |
+| Start / Back | Menu / View | Options / Create |
+| Sticks, stick clicks, D-pad | Same | Same |
+
+Face buttons and shoulders report 0 or 255 because these modern controllers
+have digital buttons. Triggers retain their analog 0–255 range. Stick Y axes
+are inverted and saturated, retaining zero at center; no additional deadzone
+is imposed because games normally apply their own.
+
+Call `xbox_InputInit()` at startup and `xbox_InputShutdown()` before `SDL_Quit()`.
+Public polls also initialize lazily. **All SDL input calls must run on the SDL/main
+thread**, since they pump host events. They do not remove window/quit events from
+the queue. Calls are not designed for concurrent use from guest worker threads.
+
+Up to four connected gamepads retain their assigned Xbox ports while attached.
+Disconnected devices are closed, and newly connected devices take the lowest
+free port. Device instance IDs prevent duplication or reassignment when device
+indices change. State packet numbers advance on an observed state change or
+new connection, rather than every poll.
+
+`xbox_InputGetState`, `xbox_InputIsConnected`, `xbox_InputGetCapabilities`, and
+`xbox_InputSetState` all refresh device presence. Unsupported vibration returns
+error 50 (`ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED`). DualSense Bluetooth extended reports are
+requested for rumble. While the game polls, active rumble is refreshed every
+500 ms with a 1000 ms bounded effect; zero motor strengths stop it. This also
+allows rumble to expire if polling stalls. SDL environment hints retain priority.
+
+Requires SDL2 2.0.18 or newer. The workspace virtual-controller test uses the
+extended virtual-device API and therefore requires SDL2 2.24 or newer. Virtual
+tests validate the compatibility mapping, not hardware Bluetooth transport,
+physical latency, or game-side integration.
